cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'CIV.IQ'
message: 'If you use CIV.IQ in your research, please cite it as below.'
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sandford
    given-names: Mark
    email: contact@civdotiq.org
repository-code: 'https://github.com/civdotiq/civ.iq'
url: 'https://civdotiq.org'
abstract: >-
  Nonpartisan civic intelligence platform connecting 29 government data
  sources and 11 open datasets to provide transparent access to
  congressional voting records, campaign finance, lobbying disclosures,
  federal spending, and legislative analysis. Includes 17 statistical
  analyzers and entity resolution across government databases.
keywords:
  - civic technology
  - government transparency
  - campaign finance
  - congressional voting
  - lobbying
  - open data
  - civic intelligence
license: Apache-2.0
version: '2.0.0'
date-released: '2025-09-02'
